# toolchain_id n_picard n_constant n_secant n_aitken n_ils n_imvj n_diag n_dense
#
# One row per FUSE_TOOLCHAIN_ID (fuse/base/config.hpp); read by
# test/num/accelerator_test.cpp, regenerated by a human running
# fuse_write_accelerator_baseline (tools/src/write_accelerator_baseline.cpp;
# see test/num/accelerator_fixtures.hpp for why this exists at all). Review
# the diff before committing a new or changed row -- this file records what
# was actually measured, not what was expected.
#
# GNU-13.3.0-nvcc_wrapper-x86_64's n_dense is -1 (did not converge within
# kMaxIters = 5000), not a typo and not a bug: SteffensenAccel's per-component
# secant step (src/num/accel_relaxation.cpp) divides by dr = r_i - r_prev_i,
# guarded only against dr being relatively zero, not against the step being
# merely huge when dr is small but nonzero. On this problem -- dense and
# off-diagonal, deliberately adversarial to Steffensen's diagonal-only
# Jacobian model, see SteffensenIsExactOnADiagonalProblemAndBasisDependent's
# own comment -- the iterate actually does converge under this toolchain, just
# at iteration 43664: confirmed separately by raising kMaxIters and watching
# the residual swing as high as 1e150 before settling, with update() never
# once returning an error. Which side of the near-zero threshold dr lands on
# at a given step is sensitive to the last bit of rounding in r_i, which is
# exactly what differs under nvcc_wrapper's host-pass codegen versus a plain
# host compiler -- a chaotic amplification of an ordinary toolchain rounding
# difference, not a divergence.
GNU-13.3.0-nvcc_wrapper-x86_64 382 382 269 57 7 7 2 -1
